# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Astro project following the latest official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 to dependencies in `package.json`
- **Updated**: `package-lock.json` with new dependencies (297 packages added)

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **Modified**: `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro`
- Added Vercel Web Analytics script tag with the `inject()` function
- Placed after the main script.js but before the affiliate tracking script
- Used the recommended Astro approach: `<script>` tag with ESM import inside

### 3. Implementation Details
The integration follows the framework-specific instructions for Astro from the official Vercel documentation:
```astro
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script>
  import { inject } from '@vercel/analytics';
  inject();
</script>
```

The script is placed in the BaseLayout component which is used by all pages, ensuring analytics tracking across the entire site.

### 4. Build Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ Analytics script is properly injected into all generated HTML files
- ✅ The bundled analytics code (~1.1kB) is present in the build output

### 5. Additional Files Updated
- `public/drug-interaction-chart.png` was regenerated as part of the standard build process

## Next Steps
After this PR is merged and deployed to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel Dashboard (Analytics tab for the project)
2. Deploy the changes to production
3. Analytics data will begin appearing in the Vercel Dashboard after deployment and user visits

## Notes
- Analytics tracking does NOT run in development mode (by design)
- The implementation adds minimal overhead (~1.1kB of JavaScript)
- The integration preserves all existing functionality including Google Analytics
- No breaking changes were introduced
